quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  7,179,"We have indeed created for Hell many of the jinn and humans: they have hearts with which they do not understand; they have eyes with which they do not see; and they have ears with which they do not hear. They are like cattle; rather, they are further astray. It is they who are heedless."
  7,180,"To Allah belong the Most Beautiful Names, so call (and supplicate) Him by them. And leave those who deviate regarding (the attributes of) His Names. Soon, they shall be recompensed for what they used to do."
  7,181,And among those whom We created is a community which guides (people) with the truth and acts justly according to it.
  7,182,"As for those who reject Our revelations, We shall gradually draw them (into destruction) in a way they cannot realise."
  7,183,"And I will grant them (a temporary) respite. Indeed, My Scheme is firmly effective."
  7,184,Have they not reflected that there is no insanity in their Guide (and that) he is only a clear Warner?
  7,185,"Have they not contemplated the dominions of the heavens, the earth, and all that Allah has created, and perhaps their end has already drawn near? So what discourse after this will they believe?"
  7,186,"Whomever Allah leaves to stray, there is no guide for him. And He leaves them alone, wandering confused in their defiance."
  7,187,"They ask you about the Hour: ‘When will it arrive?’ Say: ‘Its knowledge is only with my Lord. None but He shall reveal it at its proper time. It will be heavy upon the heavens and the earth. It will not overtake you but very suddenly.’ They ask you as if you were eager to find out. Say: ‘Its knowledge is only with Allah, but most people do not know.’"
